{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I've [G]been a wild rover
For [C]many a [G]year,
And I [G]spent all my money
On [D]whiskey and [G]beer,
But [G]now I'm returning
With [C]gold in great [G]store,
And I [G]never will [D]play
The wild [D7]rover no [G]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And it's [D]no, nay, never,
[G]No nay never no more,
Will I [C]play the wild [G]rover,
No [D]never no [G]more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I [G]went to an alehouse
I [C]used to fre[G]quent,
And I [G]told the landlady
My [D]money was [G]spent.
I [G]asked her for credit,
She [C]answered me, [G]"Nay,
Such a [G]custom as [D]yours
I could [D7]have any [G]day."
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
I [G]took from my pocket
Ten [C]sovereigns [G]bright,
And the [G]landlady's eyes
Opened [D]wide with de[G]light.
She [G]said, "I have whiskeys
And [C]wines of the [G]best,
And the [G]words that I [D]told you
Were [D7]only in [G]jest."
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
I'll go [G]home to my parents,
Con[C]fess what I've [G]done,
And I'll [G]ask them to pardon
Their [D]prodigal [G]son.
And [G]when they've caressed me
As [C]oft times be[G]fore,
I [G]never will [D]play
The wild [D7]rover no [G]more.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
